    {
      "title": "The Conjuring movie review & film summary - Roger Ebert",
      "snippet": "Watching \"The Conjuring\" is like getting a tour of a haunted house attraction from someone that pushes, and pulls you through every room. There's nothing really scary about Wan's latest because there's nothing particularly mysterious, or inviting about its proceedings. The film's relentlessly lame expository dialogue, and tedious parade of jump scares are overwhelming in the worst way possible.",
